sls — Sig Language Server
=========================

sls is a fork of ZLS (the Zig Language Server), reimagined for the Sig
toolchain and the zpm package ecosystem.

Upstream project:
  ZLS — https://github.com/zigtools/zls
  Copyright (c) ZLS contributors
  Licensed under the MIT License.

sls retains ZLS's architecture and Language Server Protocol semantics as its
starting point and rewrites the implementation in Sig, following a strict
zero-allocator, no-runtime-std-I/O design and leaning on the zpm package
library for reusable infrastructure.

Both ZLS and sls are distributed under the MIT License. The upstream copyright
notice is preserved in LICENSE alongside the sls copyright, as the MIT License
requires.
